<title>POLAND: Polish treasuries planned issues and sales for '97.</title>
<headline>Polish treasuries planned issues and sales for '97.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Finance Ministry announced on Wednesday planned sizes of treasuries issues for the whole of 1997, which are as follows.</p>
<p>NOTE: All amounts in billion zlotys.</p>
<p> ISSUE LIMIT in 1997		   40.0</p>
<p>BONDS</p>
<p>Already issued (not necessarily sold in full yet):</p>
<p>  2- and 5-year fixed bonds	    9.0</p>
<p>  1-yr index linked auction bond     4.0</p>
<p>To be issued:</p>
<p>  1-yr index linked auction bond     1.6</p>
<p>  3-year floating rate bond	    4.8</p>
<p> 10-year floating rate bond	  10.0</p>
<p> Reserve *				  10.6</p>
<p> PLANNED SALES in 1997 **	     67.16</p>
<p>  T-bills				   48.26</p>
<p>  T-bonds				   18.90 @</p>
<p>*  - reserve for increases in bond issues or for an issue of other instruments.</p>
<p>**  - in line with budget draft (includes treasuries issued in 1996 but sold only in 1997).</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
